From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] steamcompmgr: prefer an exact refresh rate over refresh doubling

_update_app_target_refresh_cycle() picks the panel rate by walking the valid
rates high-to-low and taking the first exact multiple of the target FPS:

    // Find highest mode to do refresh doubling with.
    for ( auto rate = rates.rbegin(); rate != rates.rend(); rate++ )
        if (*rate % target_fps == 0) { ... }

With {50,60,120} on the Odin 3 that means a 60fps target selects 120Hz, and a
40fps target also selects 120Hz. That is a deliberate upstream trade: a frame
held for an integer number of vblanks paces identically either way, and the
higher rate cuts latency and keeps the UI smooth.

On a battery-powered handheld the other side of that trade is often preferred
-- 60Hz on the panel rather than 120Hz is a real power saving, and the user
asking for 60 generally means the panel too. Take an exact rate when the panel
has one natively, and fall back to doubling otherwise.

Gated on a ConVar defaulting to true, so the old behaviour is one runtime
command away and the two can be A/B compared without a rebuild:

    gamescopectl prefer_exact_refresh_rate 0

Rates with no exact entry are unaffected: a 45fps target on {50,60,120} still
falls through to the doubling loop exactly as before. 50 already selected 50
because it is not a divisor of 120, so only 60 and 40 change behaviour.

--- a/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
+++ b/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
@@ -956,12 +956,20 @@
 static const uint64_t g_uDynamicRefreshDelay = 600'000'000; // 600ms
 
 static int g_nCombinedAppRefreshCycleOverride[gamescope::GAMESCOPE_SCREEN_TYPE_COUNT] = { 0, 0 };
 bool g_nCombinedAppRefreshCycleChangeRefresh[gamescope::GAMESCOPE_SCREEN_TYPE_COUNT] = { true, true };
 bool g_nCombinedAppRefreshCycleChangeFPS[gamescope::GAMESCOPE_SCREEN_TYPE_COUNT] = { true, true };
 
+// Refresh doubling runs the panel at the highest multiple of the target FPS,
+// which trades power for lower latency -- a 60fps target holds a 120Hz panel.
+// On a battery-powered handheld the opposite is often wanted, so prefer an
+// exact rate when the panel actually has one. Toggle live with:
+//     gamescopectl prefer_exact_refresh_rate 0
+gamescope::ConVar<bool> cv_prefer_exact_refresh_rate( "prefer_exact_refresh_rate", true,
+	"Prefer a refresh rate equal to the target FPS over refresh doubling." );
+
 static void _update_app_target_refresh_cycle()
 {
 	if ( !GetBackend()->GetCurrentConnector() )
 		return;
 
 	gamescope::GamescopeScreenType type = GetBackend()->GetCurrentConnector()->GetScreenType();
@@ -982,13 +990,22 @@
 	}
 
 	if ( g_nCombinedAppRefreshCycleChangeRefresh[ type ] )
 	{
 		auto rates = GetBackend()->GetCurrentConnector()->GetValidDynamicRefreshRates();
 
-		// Find highest mode to do refresh doubling with.
+		// An exact match is what the user literally asked for; take it if the
+		// panel supports that rate natively.
+		if ( cv_prefer_exact_refresh_rate &&
+		     gamescope::Algorithm::Contains( rates, uint32_t( target_fps ) ) )
+		{
+			g_nDynamicRefreshRate[ type ] = target_fps;
+			return;
+		}
+
+		// Otherwise fall back to refresh doubling: highest multiple of the target.
 		for ( auto rate = rates.rbegin(); rate != rates.rend(); rate++ )
 		{
 			if (*rate % target_fps == 0)
 			{
 				g_nDynamicRefreshRate[ type ] = *rate;
 				return;
